\subsection{Model and Inference}
\label{sec:model}

We use Qwen3-32B-FP8 \cite{qwen3-2025} served via vLLM v0.20.2 \cite{vllm-2023} on a single NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 GPU (96\,GB) with greedy decoding (temperature${}\,=\,0$, seed 42). Two NER/ED prompt versions are evaluated: v1 requests character offsets (evaluated via text matching); v2 adds format constraints, doubling precision with minimal recall loss. RE uses a single prompt version throughout. Both versions produce consistent degradation patterns; we report both where applicable to quantify formatting sensitivity \cite{sclar-sensitivity-2024} (templates in Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_prompts}). Cross-model validation uses Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct \cite{llama3-2024}. All experiments use single-seed evaluation with greedy decoding, which substantially reduces model-level randomness (residual SD = 0.88\,pp at count 80 under greedy decoding, likely attributable to FP8 quantization non-determinism); bootstrap CIs capture the remaining sampling variance from batch composition. Pair-level CIs use percentile bootstrap ($B{=}10{,}000$); batch-level CIs use $B{=}1{,}000$.
